picode provides the official Pi coding agent CLI 1.6.1 (@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent),
installed under tools/picode/.

Launcher
  Linux/macOS: tools/picode/picode
  Windows:     tools/picode\picode.cmd

Run
  picode         # interactive coding agent
  picode --help
  picode --version

The launcher keeps the current working directory as the agent workspace.

Runtime requirement
  Node.js 22.19+ is required. The launcher prefers Node from PATH and falls
  back to the nodejs22 host tool when the 'nodejs22' feature is enabled. If
  neither is usable it prints an error and exits with code 127.

Packaging note
  The npm bundle is used instead of the GitHub release binaries: those
  binaries require macOS 13+, while Node 22 (and therefore this package) runs
  on macOS 11. Dependencies are installed at packaging time with
  'npm install --omit=dev'.

Conditional nodejs22 dependency
  The manifest declares a 'nodejs22' feature whose dependency is the standalone
  host tool port nodejs22. Use the provided install.sh / install.ps1 script: it
  checks the system Node first and enables the feature only when no usable
  Node is present, so vcpkg installs nodejs22 exactly in that case.
  Example: ./install.sh --vcpkg-root /path/to/vcpkg --triplet x64-linux
  The dependency is visible with:
    vcpkg depend-info 'picode[nodejs22]' --overlay-ports=... --format=tree
